ntroduction to research, writing, and rhetorical practices employed in academic and professional contexts. The course examines the operation of genres, the audiences they address, and the purposes they serve. The course focuses on the analysis and development of student writing and rhetorical practice. Assignments include research essays, digital compositions, and oral presentations.&quot;, &quot;credits&quot;: &quot;4&quot;, &quot;grading&quot;: &quot;Graded (GRD)&quot;, &quot;typically_offered&quot;: &quot;Fall, Spring, Summer&quot;, &quot;requisites&quot;: &quot;ENG 105 non-Z Requisite&quot;, &quot;flexible&quot;: false, &quot;also_ubc&quot;: true}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\"><span class=\"box-code\">ENG 105LEC</span><span class=\"box-title\">Writing and Rhetoric</span></div><span class=\"box-credits\">4 cr</span><div class=\"box-note\">(may also be completed in a different semester shown)</div></div><div class=\"or-sep\">or</div><div class=\"box box-generic\" id=\"african-american-studies-ba__box-1-4-1\" data-detail=\"{&quot;kind&quot;: &quot;generic&quot;, &quot;category&quot;: &quot;ubc&quot;, &quot;description&quot;: &quot;Pathway: a UB Curriculum Thematic or Global Pathway course - part of at least four UB Areas/SUNY General Education categories a student&#x27;s Pathways coursework must satisfy across two Pathways (one Thematic, one Global).&quot;, &quot;catalog_url&quot;: &quot;https://www.buffalo.edu/ubcurriculum/pathways.html&quot;}\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\"><div class=\"box-eyebrow\"><span class=\"box-eyebrow-tag box-ubc-tag\">UB Curriculum</span></div><div class=\"box-label\">Pathway</div><span class=\"box-credits\">3 cr</span></div></div></div></div>\n        <div class=\"col-total\">16 or 17 credits</div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"semester-col term-fall\">\n        <div class=\"col-header\"><span class=\"col-yea